# Cloudinary Configuration (image / file storage)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The app uploads student photos, school logos and teacher documents (PDFs) to
# Cloudinary and stores the returned URL in Supabase columns
# (student_photo_url, logo_url, photo_url, file_url). The browser uses the
# public cloud name + unsigned upload preset from js/cloudinary-config.js.
#
# The API KEY + SECRET below are ONLY used by /api/cloudinary-delete (Vercel
# serverless function) to delete replaced photos/documents. They must NEVER be
# shipped in js/ — keep them as Vercel environment variables.
#
#   Vercel Dashboard → Your Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name            (e.g. dx1abc2efg)
#   CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_cloudinary_api_key
#   CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_cloudinary_api_secret
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. js/cloudinary-config.js → set CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME + an UNSIGNED upload
#      preset (Cloudinary Dashboard → Settings → Upload → Add upload preset,
#      Signing mode: Unsigned). Enable default folder "online_v" if you like.
#   2. Vercel env vars → the 3 CLOUDINARY_* values above
#
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_cloudinary_api_key
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_cloudinary_api_secret

# Resend Email Configuration
# Get your API key from https://resend.com/api-keys
# Set these as Environment Variables in your Vercel project dashboard:
#   Vercel Dashboard → Your Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@yourdomain.com
#
# Note: The RESEND_API_KEY must be set in Vercel environment variables.
# It is NOT used client-side — it's only accessed by the serverless function at /api/send-email

# Nalo Solutions SMS Gateway Configuration
# Used by the Vercel serverless function at /api/send-sms to instantly notify
# parents/guardians (SMS) the moment a fee payment is recorded in the app.
# Get your credentials from your Nalo Solutions dashboard at
# https://app.nalosolutions.com (account → API / Sender IDs).
#
#   Vercel Dashboard → Your Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#
# NALO_SMS_AUTH_KEY=your_nalo_api_auth_key     # preferred auth (key from Nalo)
# NALO_SMS_USERNAME=your_nalo_username         # fallback auth (only if no AUTH_KEY)
# NALO_SMS_PASSWORD=your_nalo_password
# NALO_SMS_SENDER_ID=YOUR_BRAND                # registered sender id (default: NALO)
#
# Note: These are ONLY accessed by the serverless function at /api/send-sms.
# The gateway endpoint used is: https://sms.nalosolutions.com/smsbackend/Resl_Nalo/send-message/
